course: dictionary
lesson: 15788
title: Not used to it yet
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unaccustomed means not used to something yet, because you have not done it or felt it often. Look for the clue in the sentence: «The city girl was unaccustomed to the cold of the farm.» She had not spent much time in cold farm weather, so she was not used to it. Ask: would "not used to" fit here? If it fits, you have found the meaning.
explain: Unaccustomed can also mean unusual, or not normal for a person. «He spoke with unaccustomed anger.» Usually he is calm, so the anger was surprising and out of character. The words around the word tell you which meaning fits.
explain: Watch for the phrase «unaccustomed to», which is followed by the thing you are not used to, such as «unaccustomed to the noise». Another phrase is «with unaccustomed», as in «with unaccustomed care», which means care that was not usual for that person.
fact: Unaccustomed means not used to something, or not normal for someone.
fact: «Unaccustomed to» is followed by the thing you are not used to: «unaccustomed to the heat».
fact: In everyday speech, people often say «not used to» instead of unaccustomed.
fact: «With unaccustomed kindness» means kindness that was not usual for that person.
fact: Unaccustomed is a formal word, so you will meet it more in books than in talk.
exercise: «Ravi was unaccustomed to the cold of the mountains.» What does unaccustomed mean? | Warmly dressed for it | *Not used to it | Very happy about it | Sure about it
exercise: «Her teacher spoke with unaccustomed patience, and the class was surprised.» What does unaccustomed mean here? | Very fast | *Not usual for her | Fully used to it | Loud and angry
exercise: «The lamb was unaccustomed to the rain.» Which word tells you the lamb had not felt rain often? | rain | *unaccustomed | lamb | the
test: «After months in the city, Maya felt unaccustomed to the quiet of the countryside.» What does unaccustomed mean? | Happy to be there | *Not used to it | Very calm and peaceful | Bored of the same place
test: Which phrase means a person is not used to something? | Accustomed to the noise | Eager for the noise | *Unaccustomed to the noise | Afraid of noise and loud sounds
exam: «With unaccustomed silence, the usually chatty parrot said nothing all day.» What does unaccustomed mean here? | *Not used to it for long | Very loud | Not usual for the parrot | Bright and colourful
